build_parent no longer records which of a level's children an inner node
of the next level has adopted: a failure partway frees those children twice,
once under their parent and once from the level. Caught under ASan.
Guarded-by: "alloc sweep: a bulk build that fails partway frees each node once"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/btree.cppm b/bytecaskdb/btree.cppm
index 81244aa..83607ba 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/btree.cppm
+++ b/bytecaskdb/btree.cppm
@@ -1709,7 +1709,6 @@ protected:
       auto &from = levels_[lvl];
       adopt_child(lvl + 1, inner,
                   i == 0 ? std::vector<std::byte>{} : std::move(from.seps[i - 1]));
-      from.adopted = j;
       i = j;
     }
     levels_[lvl] = Level{};
